iew.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/19/419819/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7b3a3e6ae10438b00c70e93e29ca250c05cfd2a4" commit="ce9ea9b8c9f9d1c40380da2bb2095599cc46dbc2" commit_message="[autotest] Distinguish &quot;get_version&quot; from &quot;get_image_name&quot;  For CrOS builds, the AFE class for access to the get_stable_versions RPC functions was formatting the stable version as a complete image name, not just a version number.  This was a problem for two reasons:   * Some callers needed the version number, not the formatted image     name.   * The get_version() method was returning values inconsistent with     the behavior of get_all_versions() and set_version(), both of     which use version numbers.  This changes the get_version() method to return a version string, and adds a new get_image_name() method for returning the image name. It also converts callers that need an image name to use the new method.  BUG=chromium:673836 TEST=Manually invoke the new method from python CLI  Change-Id: I7b3a3e6ae10438b00c70e93e29ca250c05cfd2a4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/419329 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="419329" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/29/419329/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5d296657da7c6561da86266724692f9659c15163" commit="01d1c5b05ee0f4114614514cbcf797fb90ad1751" commit_message="security_ASLR: Make finding processes more robust  There have been a few flaky runs where the first line of `pidof ${name}` is not the process we were looking for